      en: "The Bahrain International Investment Park (BIIP) is a state-of-the-art industrial park located in Hidd, in close proximity to Khalifa Bin Salman Port and Bahrain International Airport. Opened in 2005, the park covers an area of 2.5 million square meters and was designed to attract foreign direct investment into export-oriented manufacturing and service companies. The BIIP offers investors first-class infrastructure, including pre-built industrial facilities and serviced land plots. Key benefits include 100% foreign ownership, tax exemptions, and a duty-free zone that facilitates access to the entire GCC market. The park is home to a variety of international companies from sectors such as food processing, electronics, medical technology, and logistics, making it a cornerstone of Bahrain's economic diversification strategy."
